  "content": {
    "title": "How to Watch Justin Bieber, Sabrina Carpenter, Karol G, and More at Coachella",
    "text": "4 min readSpringtime is here, marking the arrival of music festival season, which will kick off this weekend with the 25th edition of Coachella. It used to be that if you weren’t in the Valley to live the experience IRL, all you could do was live vicariously through photos of people’s outfits, but thanks to the modern advent of the livestream, you can still enjoy all the performances from your favorite artist from the comfort of your own home. This year, the festival organizers have expanded their offering. Not only is it being streamed in 4K, you can even watch artists from up to four different stages simultaneously, and if you’re watching on your phone, there is also a dedicated vertical stream. For those who will actually plan out their weekend around set times, there’s a Coachella app where you can organize your dream weekend and get notifications on when it’s time to lock in. And because we love to be servicey, here’s a guide to the bands and artists we’ll be keeping our eye on this weekend.Frazer Harrison//Getty ImagesSabrina Carpenter at Coachella in 2024Weekend 1: Friday, April 103:00 p.m. PT/6:00 p.m. EST: Slayyter on the Mojave StageThe up-and-coming pop/dance/electronic artist has quickly become an IYKYK name, with her latest record, Worst Girl in America, topping the American Billboard dance charts.3:45 p.m. PT/6:45 p.m. EST: Groove Armada on the Yuma StageThis ’90s electronic duo made up of Andy Cato and Tom Findlay broke through the scene with a slew of hits, including 1999’s “I See You Baby.” Most recently, they teamed up with Pink Pantheress to remix her song “Stateside.”6:40 p.m. PT/9:40 p.m. EST: Dijon on the Outdoor TheaterLast year, Dijon contributed to songs on both Justin Bieber’s Swag and Bon Iver’s Sable Fable—enough for any artist to call it a good year. He released his second solo album, Baby, which topped many of the year’s best-of lists.7:00 p.m. PT/10:00 p.m. EST: The xx on the Coachella StageFor many, the xx completely defined the sound of the early 2010s. The trio, made of Romy, Jamie xx, and Oliver Sim, have released two more critically acclaimed albums—with another rumored to be on the way.8:00 p.m. PT/11:00 p.m. EST: Katseye on the Sahara StageAdvertisement - Continue Reading BelowThe girl group born out of the Dream Academy TV show, made up of Daniela Avanzini, Lara Raj, Megan Skiendiel, Sophia Laforteza, and Yoonchae Jeung, is making its Coachella debut this year. (Fan favorite Manon Bannerman remains “on hiatus” and will not be joining the performance.)9:05 p.m. PT/12:00 p.m. EST: Sabrina Carpenter on the Coachella StageFresh off the release of “Pretty Girl Avenue,” her latest single off Man’s Best Friend, Sabrina Carpenter returns to the Coachella stage for the second time as headliner.Kevin Winter//Getty ImagesJustin Bieber at Coachella 2022Weekend 1: Saturday, April 113:00 p.m. PT/6:00 p.m. EST: Jack White on the Mojave StageFresh off his performances on SNL last weekend, the ex–White Stripe and Detroit rock royalty is back on the Coachella stage for the third time.5:30 p.m. PT/8:30 p.m. EST: Addison Rae on the Coachella StageCertified fashion girlie Addison Rae, whose self-titled debut is definitely one of those rare all-killer/no-filler records, is bringing all her bops to the main Coachella stage.6:15 p.m. PT/9:15 p.m. EST: Geese on the Gobi StageResponsible for Getting Killed, one of the best records of 2025, Geese, a.k.a. the rock band to define a generation, will be playing Coachella for the first time.7:05 p.m. PT/10:05 p.m. EST: Sombr on the Outdoor TheatreNew York singer-songwriter Sombr was nominated for a Best New Artist Grammy following the release of his album I Barely Know Her. Expect to see the 20-year-old croon and pull a great look onstage this Saturday.8:00 p.m. PT/11:00 p.m. EST: Nine Inch Noize on the Sahara StageNine Inch Noize is what you get when you combine Nine Inch Nails’s Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross with the German producer and DJ Boyz Noise. Get ready to rave.9:00 p.m. PT/12:00 p.m. EST: The Strokes on the Main Coachella StageThe Strokes are back on the Coachella stage a few days after announcing the June release of Reality Awaits, their long-awaited follow-up to 2020’s The New Abnormal. 10:15 p.m. PT/1:15 a.m. EST: Interpol on the Mojave StageYes, it’ll be late for us East Coasters, but we’re certainly staying up to watch Interpol after the Strokes and continue to relive the golden era of the early-aughts music scene.11:25 p.m. PT/2:25 a.m. EST: Justin Bieber on the Coachella StageJustin Bieber is the headliner for the festival’s second night, and if his Grammys performance was any indication, we’re set to witness another indelible performance.Christopher Polk//Getty ImagesKarol G performing in 2024Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowWeekend 1: Sunday, April 124:45 p.m. PT/7:45 p.m. EST: Wet Leg on the Coachella StageWet Leg, the British indie band, made a splash stateside after one of its songs appeared in an episode of Heated Rivalry. (If you’re not familiar, check out the band’s excellent Tiny Desk performance.)8:00 p.m. PT/11:00 p.m. EST: Fatboy Slim on the Quasar StageNeed a dance break? Fatboy’s Slim got you.8:40 p.m. PT/11:40 p.m. EST: Laufey on the Outdoor TheatreThe Icelandic singer Laufey won a Grammy for last year’s A Matter of Time. Another fashion-favorite singer, she will no doubt stage a dreamy performance.9:55 p.m. PT/12:55 a.m. EST: Karol G on the Coachella StageThe Colombian superstar Karol G is the first Latinx woman to headline the festival. Come for the good vibes and stay for a little Spanish lesson!See the full lineup below:",
